# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Node / frontend build output
node_modules/
web/dist/
web/dist-pages/

# Scratch directory written by the TanStack Router Vite plugin
web/.tanstack/

# TypeScript incremental build cache
*.tsbuildinfo

# Built console, embedded into the binary with -tags embed_spa
internal/spa/dist/

# Local build artifacts
bin/

# Coverage output (vitest writes a directory; go writes *.out, covered above)
coverage/

# Working notes for the in-progress cleanup pass: an architecture walkthrough
# and an audit findings list. Deliberately local -- they describe a half-done
# state and would be misleading in the repo until the open items are closed.
# Delete these two lines to publish them.
docs/
